WEBVTT

00:00:28.871 --> 00:00:30.038
How are they performed?

00:00:30.079 --> 00:00:32.204
And how do we know 
whether they’re reliable?

00:00:32.246 --> 00:00:35.037
When it comes to dietary 
or medical information,

00:00:35.079 --> 00:00:36.371
the first thing to remember

00:00:36.412 --> 00:00:38.912
is that while studies 
on animals or individual cells

00:00:38.954 --> 00:00:41.121
can point the way 
towards further research,

00:00:41.162 --> 00:00:44.204
the only way to know 
how something will affect humans

00:00:44.246 --> 00:00:46.496
is through a study 
involving human subjects.

00:00:46.537 --> 00:00:48.246
And when it comes to human studies,

00:00:48.287 --> 00:00:51.579
the scientific gold standard 
is the Randomized Clinical Trial or RCT.

00:00:51.621 --> 00:00:53.912
The key to RCTs is that the subjects

00:00:53.954 --> 00:00:56.746
are randomly assigned
to their study groups.

00:00:56.787 --> 00:00:59.579
They are often blinded 
to make them more rigorous.

00:00:59.621 --> 00:01:02.912
This process attempts to ensure
the only difference between the groups